<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.3.4: Identifying Best Fit Line for Residuals on a Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00730</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.3.4: Identifying Best Fit Line for Residuals on a Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a241e6ae-ebcc-469d-9df3-3c9e419e057e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Each of these graphs of residuals is from the same set of data using different lines to fit the data.
    Which graph is most likely to represent the residuals from a line of best fit? Be prepared to show your
    reasoning.</para>
   
        
    <div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-evenly">
      <para>Graph A<figure><media alt="Graph of residuals, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/51c73a9fda2fbdbcb41a323a4392cdf78f0b5e58"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Graph B<figure><media alt="Graph of residuals, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b180a0f640c1a1fe9cf4265fcbe68c26f9613b33"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Graph C<figure><media alt="Graph of residuals, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a11d22edae507f7e59f2e75a9bd4650fc903a9ce"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Graph D<figure><media alt="Graph of residuals, origin O."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/6413df0124f8e7464eb418a28a133b866228e7b9"/></media></figure></para>
  </div>    
      <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
      <para>Graph A is most likely to represent the residuals from the best fit line. The residuals seem well
          spaced on either side of the \(x\)-axis without an obvious pattern, and all of the residuals are close to
          0.</para>
      <title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
      <title>Points to Emphasize</title>
      <para>If students struggle here, select sample student work to discuss and assign practice problems to revisit this
        topic. Residuals will not be discussed again in this unit.</para>
</section>
</content>
